x_comment(x_InventionStroboscopy1931,"Edgerton began work on the electronic flash lamp in 1928.  He started with mercury filled flash lamps and achieved durations as short as 1 microsecond.\n\nIn WWII, he moved on to high speed motion photography, employing an electrical contactor driven by the sprocket moving the film, thereby achieving 6000 frames per second.\n\nIn the early 50's he addressed photography of nuclear blasts, which were too intense for traditional photography.\n\nIn 1958, he worked on photographing rocket shockwaves, using light reflected from a scotchlite screen and refracted by the shockwaves, yielding a visible shadow on film.") :- x_cid(a65b132bac18f7).
